# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Re-arms what each hand held, out of the backpack, when a cast or a disarm empties it.
# Hands are recorded at Play, before recovery can cast, then every two seconds. Each
# layer keeps its serial across Plays. A missing item is forgotten, and a replacement
# seen on that layer takes over. No label or weapon table is needed.
# With no remembered item, rearm_graphic picks from the backpack. Its pending serial
# stays fixed until a hand confirms it or it leaves the backpack. The first request
# uses lefthand, as hotkey/weapon-katana does. The actual layer is read after the equip.
# An equip request is not proof of success. In-game checks: Open items part 16.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ config
#
#   config__rearm_graphic
#      Graphic of the weapon to pick out of the backpack while both hands are empty and
#      nothing is remembered. 0 disables that search. A chosen serial is retried until
#      a hand confirms it or it leaves the backpack. Graphics: document/game/item-list.md.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__rearm_graphic 0


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ wait
#
#   interval__equip_retry
#      How often the hands are read. A refused equip, after a disarm for example, waits
#      this long before the next try.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! interval__equip_retry 2000


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ timer
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
timer__equip interval__equip_retry


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ state
#
#   var__rearm_left, var__rearm_right
#      The serial last seen on the two-handed layer (lefthand) and on the one-handed layer
#      (righthand), kept across Stop and Play. 0 means nothing seen yet, or the item gone
#      from hand and backpack.
#
#   var__rearm_pending
#      Backpack choice awaiting a hand observation, not a confirmed equip. Cleared on
#      Play, when an item is seen in hand, or when this choice leaves the backpack.
#
#   var__rearm_sent
#      Scratch: 1 once this check sent an equip, so the second hand waits for the next.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
if not varexist var__rearm_left
    @setvar! var__rearm_left 0
endif

if not varexist var__rearm_right
    @setvar! var__rearm_right 0
endif

@setvar! var__rearm_pending 0
@setvar! var__rearm_sent 0


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ setup
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Snapshot before the first recovery pass. Empty hands retain the previous serials.
if findlayer self lefthand as alias__rearm_left
    @setvar! var__rearm_left alias__rearm_left

    if config__sysmsg = 1
        sysmsg "Rearm: two-handed layer remembered, serial={{alias__rearm_left}}." 88
    endif
endif

if findlayer self righthand as alias__rearm_right
    @setvar! var__rearm_right alias__rearm_right

    if config__sysmsg = 1
        sysmsg "Rearm: one-handed layer remembered, serial={{alias__rearm_right}}." 88
    endif
endif


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ loop
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # REARM
    #
    # Every two seconds. Arming before a cast completes interrupts the cast (wiki Combat
    # Overview), so casting, a cursor, the item queue and hiding block this. Each layer:
    # an item in hand is remembered once by serial, an empty hand gets its remembered
    # item back out of the backpack, and a remembered item in neither place is forgotten.
    # One equip per check, the two-handed layer first. With both hands empty and nothing
    # remembered, rearm_graphic names the one to pick. The request is not proof of the
    # equip: the next check reads the hands again.
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    if timer "timer__equip" >= interval__equip_retry
        if not hidden and not queued and not casting and not targetexists
            settimer "timer__equip" 0
            @setvar! var__rearm_sent 0

            if findlayer self lefthand as alias__rearm_left
                @setvar! var__rearm_pending 0

                if var__rearm_left != alias__rearm_left
                    @setvar! var__rearm_left alias__rearm_left

                    if config__sysmsg = 1
                        sysmsg "Rearm: two-handed layer remembered, serial={{alias__rearm_left}}." 88
                    endif
                endif
            elseif var__rearm_left != 0
                if find var__rearm_left backpack as alias__rearm_packed
                    # lift waits for the held item. The retry timer spaces the next hand check,
                    # so a refused equip after a disarm does not stall recovery.
                    lift alias__rearm_packed
                    drop self lefthand
                    @setvar! var__rearm_sent 1

                    if config__sysmsg = 1
                        sysmsg "Rearm: equip requested on the two-handed layer, serial={{alias__rearm_packed}}. The next check reads the hands." 88
                    endif

                    wait wait__short
                else
                    @setvar! var__rearm_left 0
                endif
            endif

            if var__rearm_sent = 0
                if findlayer self righthand as alias__rearm_right
                    @setvar! var__rearm_pending 0

                    if var__rearm_right != alias__rearm_right
                        @setvar! var__rearm_right alias__rearm_right

                        if config__sysmsg = 1
                            sysmsg "Rearm: one-handed layer remembered, serial={{alias__rearm_right}}." 88
                        endif
                    endif
                elseif var__rearm_right != 0
                    if find var__rearm_right backpack as alias__rearm_packed
                        lift alias__rearm_packed
                        drop self righthand
                        @setvar! var__rearm_sent 1

                        if config__sysmsg = 1
                            sysmsg "Rearm: equip requested on the one-handed layer, serial={{alias__rearm_packed}}. The next check reads the hands." 88
                        endif

                        wait wait__short
                    else
                        @setvar! var__rearm_right 0
                    endif
                endif
            endif

            if var__rearm_sent = 0 and config__rearm_graphic != 0 and var__rearm_left = 0 and var__rearm_right = 0 and lhandempty and rhandempty
                if not find var__rearm_pending backpack
                    @setvar! var__rearm_pending 0

                    if findtype config__rearm_graphic backpack as alias__rearm_pick
                        @setvar! var__rearm_pending alias__rearm_pick
                    endif
                endif

                if find var__rearm_pending backpack as alias__rearm_found
                    # Keep the choice separate from the confirmed hand serials.
                    lift alias__rearm_found
                    drop self lefthand

                    if config__sysmsg = 1
                        sysmsg "Rearm: graphic {{config__rearm_graphic}} picked from the backpack, serial={{alias__rearm_found}}. The next check reads the hands." 88
                    endif

                    wait wait__short
                elseif timer "timer__message" >= interval__message
                    overhead "[ weapon, out ]" 254
                    settimer "timer__message" 0
                endif
            endif
        endif
    endif
